Homepage: https://github.com/mawena/Voix-la
Description: dub videos with a cloned voice, using the free Kaggle GPU
 Voix-là replaces the voice of a video (a song, a duet, rap or speech) with
 a cloned voice, and gives back the same video and its audio.
 .
 The heavy work runs on the free GPU of the user's own Kaggle account, in a
 private dataset and a private kernel: voice separation, voice cleaning (lead
 and backing vocals split, original reverb removed), automatic choice between
 singing and speech, one octave shift per singer, and conversion with
 YingMusic-SVC or Seed-VC. Mixing (following the dynamics of the original
 voice, de-esser, reverb, true-peak limiter) and putting the sound back on the
 video run locally with ffmpeg and numpy; picture and subtitles are copied
 without re-encoding. An optional auto-tune version, from subtle pitch
 correction to a robotic effect in the key detected from the music, is made
 locally too, with x42-autotune (recommended package x42-plugins).
 .
 Includes the `doubler` command and the "Voix-là" GTK 4 and libadwaita
 application: voices (from a file or the microphone), dubbing queue, results
 with original/dubbed playback at the same position, machine and Kaggle
 status.
 .
 Needs a Kaggle account with GPU access, its API token, and the kaggle
 command-line tool, which is not packaged: install it in a Python virtual
 environment (see the README). The YingMusic-SVC weights are CC BY-NC 4.0:
 personal, non-commercial use only.

